  "description": "Three plates turn on one hub — teeth on the outer one — each carrying twelve coloured beads in its housings, over the twelve rays drawn between the hub and the rim. Drag a plate and it turns alone; the other two hold. Rays that would pay light up under the beads while you turn, so a plate is never moved blind, and the dial only cashes them once it comes to rest. A paid ray is re-fed from outside the rim, and the beads that fly in can land on a ray of their own, so one move can keep paying long after you let go. Every four rays the hub's meter buys a special bead, and a move that pays two rays at once — or a chain at x8 — buys a bigger one. There are eight of them and no level ever carries the whole catalogue: a CHARGE unzips the plate it sits on, a NOVA is wild and takes its colour off the entire dial, a BOMB clears the board outright, a FIRE takes the two rays either side, a LASER fires through the hub and out the far side, a SCORE bead arms an x2, x5 or x10 window, a SLOW bead holds the eclipse back — and an ICE bead, the one you do not want, freezes the plate it breaks on. The thirty levels introduce them one at a time and run in five worlds, each with its own material for the beads and its own palette for the machine.",
